rly Umbrian inscriptions, adapting them to modern phonological rules. This translation attempts to do so, creating a term that feels both new and authentically Umbrian. The capitalization of 'Dìgitâl' follows conventions for loanwords in Umbrian orthography.  Further, the term is intended to be used in conjunction with explanatory phrases when first introduced in academic texts, clarifying its meaning within the context of Digital Humanities practices."
}
